# A run is published by being named, not by which machine produced it: the CLI
# writes ad-hoc runs as `<timestamp>-<model>.json`, so `baseline-` is the mark
# of one somebody chose to keep.
#
# `results/baseline-*.json` is the current cohort: one commit, clean tree, one
# run per model, enforced by `pnpm run guard:benchmark-cohort`. Superseded
# cohorts move to `results/history/` rather than being overwritten — a model
# getting worse across commits is worth being able to see, and it is the one
# thing overwriting destroys.
results/*
!results/baseline-*.json
!results/history/
!results/history/*.json
dist/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Built by `pnpm run build:viewer`; the source of truth is viewer/broadcast/src/.
viewer/broadcast/dist/
